WorkflowRegistry.upsertWorkflow
├── When msg sender is NOT a linked owner
│   └── It should revert with with OwnershipLinkDoesNotExist
├── When msg sender IS a linked owner
    ├── When no existing record for owner name tag combination // _createWorkflow
    │   ├── When the input is not valid
    │   │   ├── When workflowName length is 0
    │   │   │   └── It should It should revert with with WorkflowNameRequired
    │   │   ├── When workflowName length is greater than 64
    │   │   │   └── It should revert with WorkflowNameTooLong
    │   │   ├── When tag length is 0
    │   │   │   └── It should revert with WorkflowTagRequired
    │   │   ├── When tag length is greater than 32
    │   │   │   └── It should revert with WorkflowTagTooLong
    │   │   ├── When workflowId is 0
    │   │   │   └── It should revert with ZeroAddressNotAllowed
    │   │   ├── When workflowId already exists
    │   │   │   └── It should revert with WorkflowIDAlreadyExists
    │   │   ├── When binaryUrl is greater than 200
    │   │   │   └── It should revert with URLTooLong
    │   │   ├── When configUrl is greater than 200
    │   │   │   └── It should revert with URLTooLong
    │   │   └── When attributes is greater than 512
    │   │       └── It should revert with AttributesTooLong
    │   └─ When the input is valid
    │      ├── When keepAlive is true
    │      │   └── It skip pausing existing workflows with same owner, name
    │      ├── When keepAlive is false
    │      │   ├── When ther eare more than one other active workflows with the same workflow key
    │      │   │   └── It pause each of those before proceeding
    │      │   └── When none share the key
    │      │       └── It does not pause any workflows
    │      ├── When the status is active
    │      │   ├── When global DON cap reached
    │      │   │   └── It should revert with MaxWorkflowsPerDONExceeded
    │      │   └── When user-per-DON cap reached
    │      │       └── It should revert with MaxWorkflowsPerUserDONExceeded
    │      └── When creating a new record
    │          └── It should write the new s_workflows[rid], update all necessary counters, and emit WorkflowRegistered
    └── When an existing record at rid exists // _updateWorkflow  
        ├── When the inputs are not valid
        │   ├── When newWorkflowId is 0  
        │   │   └── It should revert with  ZeroAddressNotAllowed
        │   ├── When newWorkflowId already exists
        │   │   └── It should revert with  WorkflowIDAlreadyExists(newWorkflowId)  
        │   ├── When newBinaryURL is greater than 200 or configURL is greater than 200
        │   │   └── It should revert with  URLTooLong
        │   └── When newAttributes is greater than 512  
        │       └── It should revert with  AttributesTooLong
        └── When the inputs are valid 
            ├── It should update the records and remap the indices
            └── It should emit WorkflowUpdated
└── When any of the steps fails
    └── It should roll back all state changes, indices, and skip event emissions.
